<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">
    Channel probe <span class="font-mono text-base font-normal text-zinc-500">{@room}</span>
  </h1>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500">
    Plain JavaScript client on <code>/socket</code> — no LiveView involved, and no
    long-poll fallback. If this page connects, WebSockets survive the Worker and
    Durable Object hop.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 p-4 text-sm">
    <p class="text-zinc-500">Share this session</p>
    <input
      id="share-url"
      type="text"
      readonly
      value={@probe_url}
      class="mt-2 w-full rounded-md border border-zinc-300 bg-zinc-50 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-xs"
    />
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-zinc-500">
      Anyone opening that link joins this room. The LiveView client for the same room is at <a
        href={@share_url}
        class="underline"
      >{@share_url}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div id="channel-probe" data-room={@room} class="mt-8">
    <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-4 gap-y-2 rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 p-4 text-sm">
      <dt class="text-zinc-500">Socket state</dt>
      <dd id="probe-state" class="font-mono">connecting…</dd>
      <dt class="text-zinc-500">Transport</dt>
      <dd id="probe-transport" class="font-mono">—</dd>
      <dt class="text-zinc-500">Nickname</dt>
      <dd id="probe-nickname" class="font-mono">—</dd>
      <dt class="text-zinc-500">Round trip</dt>
      <dd id="probe-rtt" class="font-mono">—</dd>
      <dt class="text-zinc-500">Reconnects</dt>
      <dd id="probe-reconnects" class="font-mono">0</dd>
      <dt class="text-zinc-500">Node uptime</dt>
      <dd id="probe-uptime" class="font-mono">—</dd>
      <dt class="text-zinc-500">Persistence</dt>
      <dd id="probe-durability" class="font-mono">—</dd>
    </dl>

    <form id="probe-form" class="mt-6 flex gap-2">
      <input
        id="probe-input"
        type="text"
        name="body"
        placeholder="Say something"
        autocomplete="off"
        required
        maxlength="2000"
        class="flex-1 rounded-md border border-zinc-300 px-3 py-2 text-sm focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-zinc-500"
      />
      <button
        type="submit"
        class="rounded-md bg-zinc-900 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-zinc-700"
      >
        Send
      </button>
    </form>

    <ul id="probe-messages" class="mt-6 divide-y divide-zinc-200 border-t border-zinc-200 text-sm">
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-zinc-500">
    Messages sent here must appear in the LiveView client above, which proves PubSub fan-out
    between two different socket implementations.
  </p>
</div>
